{"id": "effect-794ba073-967c-58b8-9c88-ee3d045b46d8", "sessionId": "341d9e81-6e08-2061-eb77-520faea41e81", "turnId": "turn-542b409187d41a418292618329863619", "createdAt": 1792350094647, "updatedAt": 1792350094763, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\checkpoint.md", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\checkpoint.md", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\checkpoint.md", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\checkpoint.md", "offset": null, "limit": 2000}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\checkpoint.md", "content": "# Slice 3 implementation checkpoint\n\nWritten by the Mistral implementation owner. Living checkpoint; updated as\nwork proceeds. Policy ANY_ECOSYSTEM_RISK_PROPORTIONATE_ENGINEERING_V1 rev\n2026-09-24.2. Current assignment: SLICE3_UNBLOCK_DELIVERY.md (same owner,\nMaxTurns80, checkpoint by turn12, handoff by turn60, final15 reserved).\n\n## Status: unblock-and-deliver run — EARLY SCIENTIFIC/DESIGN CHECKPOINT\n\nBudget: 1486.0224586999684 s used of 3600 s; 900 s final reserve untouched.\nTHIS assignment permits at most 450 ADDITIONAL process-wall seconds of\nproduct numerical checks through harness.py (shared ledger, not renewed\nauthority; no --allow-reserve). Per diagnostic 120 s; pytest regression up\nto 600 s only if remaining assignment and task allowance permit. One\nnumerical child at a time. No mesh/arc/final25 runs. No Git mutations,\nsiblings or workers. 0 additional seconds spent so far this assignment.\n\n### Findings so far (this run)\n\n1. DC1 and DC2 are FIXED in src/anysolver/nonlinear_static.py (syntax-\n   verified by ast.parse; not yet numerically verified):\n   - DC1: the subdivision retry now requires a strictly positive finite\n     attempted span (np.isfinite, > 0.0), keeps the geometric min-span\n     floor, and adds an explicit per-interval cutback-count bound\n     (cutbacks_this_step < max_control_cutbacks). A zero-span request runs\n     its bounded Newton attempt and exits through the finite\n     minimum_control_step_reached/stopped_at_limit path.\n   - DC2: step_iterations resets after each accepted publication when a\n     subdivided interval continues, so per-record iteration counts describe\n     only their own accepted increment; solve-wide totals remain in\n     total_iterations and the cumulative control_attempts/control_cutbacks\n     fields.\n2. Recorded evidence slice3-continuation-achievable-1 (junit.xml, no new\n   numerical cost) is already discriminating for item 3:\n   - half[direct] at -0.10 PASSES the complete oracle including the physical\n     support-vs-applied wrench balance at 1e-6 relative (applied scale\n     61917 N/Nm).\n   - half[interp] at -0.10 fails ONLY the wrench balance:\n     12.876526860967095 vs 1e-6*61917.19850912096 (2.08e-4 relative), while\n     its independently reconstructed reduced residual passed the 1e-7 gate\n     and the solve completed at the target.\n   The identical transfer/recovery machinery passes for direct and fails\n   only for interp, whose sole kinematic difference is the weighted\n   rotation-vector average theta_bar = sum w_i theta_i across two masters\n   with distinct finite rotations. This is consistent with cause (a)\n   (non-covariance of the linearly averaged rotation vector) and weighs\n   against cause (b) (a constituent work-map/recovery defect), which would\n   affect direct equally.\n\n### Rigid-spin objectivity derivation (item 3, before any mechanics change)\n\nContract adopted by Astra: under a superposed rigid rotation Q the weighted\ndeformed attachment point and the slave orientation must transform as\n\n  x_b(u^Q) = Q x_b(u),   R_b(u^Q) = Q R_b(u),\n\nwith the existing linearized weights and the exact direct/identical-rotation\nlimit retained.\n\nCurrent map (corotational.NonlinearRotatingMPCMap):\n\n  x_b = sum_i w_i x_i + (R(theta_bar) - I) r_0,  theta_b = theta_bar,\n  theta_bar = sum_i w_i theta_i  (linear average of rotation vectors).\n\nUnder a superposed spin Q (rotation vector psi), master states transform\nequivariantly: x_i -> Q x_i, R(theta_i) -> Q R(theta_i), i.e.\ntheta_i -> log(Q exp(theta_i^)), which is NOT theta_i + psi unless all\nrotations share the axis of Q. Therefore\n\n  R(theta_bar(u^Q)) = R(sum_i w_i log(Q exp(theta_i^)))\n                != Q R(sum_i w_i theta_i)   in general,\n\nbecause exp(sum w_i log(Q R_i)) != Q exp(sum w_i log R_i): the log map is\nonly affine on commuting rotations. The translation part sum w_i x_i is\nequivariant (translations are linear), so the attachment point x_b fails\nequivariance only through the (R(theta_bar)-I) r_0 term, and the\norientation theta_b fails directly. For a single master (direct, w=1)\ntheta_bar = theta_1 and R(theta_b(u^Q)) = Q R(theta_1) exactly: the map IS\nequivariant, matching the recorded direct pass. For interp with distinct\nmaster rotations the failure is O(|psi| x master-rotation contrast x lever\narm); the reduced residual J^T(imbalance) can still be driven to 1e-7 (the\nconstraint holds in the reduced metric) while the transferred physical\nwrench retains a non-objective residual moment (12.8765 Nm at 61917 scale)\nthat cannot cancel the applied wrench at 1e-6.\n\nDiscriminating check to implement (cheap, no FE solve): a global rigid-spin\nequivariance probe of the map itself. Construct a master state with distinct\nfinite master rotations, superpose Q = exp(psi) with generic psi, and\nmeasure e_pos = ||x_b(u^Q) - Q x_b(u)|| and\ne_rot = ||log(R_b(u^Q)^T Q R_b(u))||. Direct: machine precision. Interp:\nsignificantly nonzero, growing with |psi| and master-rotation contrast.\nPlus a virtual-work covariance probe: the transferred master wrench of the\nspun state must equal the Q-transform of the original transferred wrench;\nthe non-objective average violates this for interp only. This converts the\ncircumstantial direct-vs-interp evidence into direct kinematic\ndiscrimination before any mechanics change.\n\n### Candidate design: objective SO(3) mean (proposal for Astra review)\n\nIf the probe confirms cause (a), replace the non-objective average on the\nACTIVE rotating-offset route only (legacy/linearized relations unchanged)\nwith an intrinsic weighted SO(3) mean:\n\n  R_bar = argmin_R sum_i w_i ||log(R^T R_i)||^2,\n\nby the standard barycentric fixed-point iteration in the mean's tangent\nspace, with theta_bar := log(R_bar). Connected treatment required by the\nmap's other members:\n\n- apply_kinematics/to_linear_displacement: offset (R_bar - I) r_0 and\n  slave orientation theta_b = log(R_bar); the inverse restart map uses the\n  same mean.\n- jacobian: du_b/dq gains dR_bar/dtheta_i through the mean's tangent\n  weights W_i, composed with the existing lever-arm Jacobian A(theta_bar);\n  the slave rotation rows gain sum_i W_i dtheta_i/dq.\n- reduce_force: master rotation covectors receive the transpose of the\n  mean's tangent block applied to the slave moment covector (in addition\n  to the existing delta_A^T f_b term).\n- geometric_tangent: rotating_mpc_geometric_hessian at theta_bar = log\n  R_bar plus the mean-curvature hessian term.\n- transfer_slave_imbalance_to_masters: distribute the slave moment through\n  the mean's tangent weights (not the linear w_i) so the physical wrench\n  oracle stays the transpose of the actual kinematics.\n- Limits: exact for a single master (reduces to direct), exact for\n  identical master rotations, consistent with the linearized weights to\n  first order (small-rotation/public linearized relation unchanged).\n  Constraint postchecks, inverse restart mapping and downstream nonlinear\n  rotation dependency refusals must be re-admitted against the new map.\n\nThis is candidate design within the adopted objective; Astra reviews\nscientific applicability before adoption. No mechanics change is made in\nthis run without that review; the probe only demonstrates the defect.\n\n### Intended remaining edits (this run)\n\n1. DC bounded residual line search on the adaptive rotating-MPC route only\n   (trial evaluations replace the pending state candidate and are never\n   committed; committed histories retained; bounded 8 halvings; fall back\n   to the full Newton step when no reduction improves the merit).\n2. Ordinary-resume lambda recovery as a Newton guess inside\n   _solve_static_displacement_control (least-squares scalar from the copied\n   initial state, rotating route, ordinary supplied initial-state route\n   only; no public API/success-criterion change).\n3. D1 declared-class spy regression (monkeypatched factorize recording\n   MatrixClass and delegating unchanged; independent of optional PARDISO).\n4. Bounded zero-span restart regression (EP fixture, restart at the current\n   controlled value, max_iterations=1: must terminate with a finite failure\n   status, not retry forever).\n5. T2/T3/T4 acceptance-gap closures in the continuation module\n   (every-snapshot reconstruction at achieved lambda with\n   max(norm(J^T lam F),1) normalization, full GP/fiber history comparison\n   at split/milestones/final, named deep copies observed on\n   rejection/cancellation, milestone-based comparison, no empty conditional\n   passes).\n6. Rigid-spin equivariance probe as a diagnostic script + recorded run.\n\n### Actual artifacts at assignment start (from evidence, not plans)\n\n- 31 charged attempts in budget.json; latest was\n  slice3-continuation-achievable-1 (EXIT_1, 39.234439099993324 s,\n  cumulative 1486.0224586999684 s).\n- tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py: 16 passes\n  (slice3-repairs-5) on the then-current source. Do not rerun unchanged\n  source16.\n- EP continuation module: 7 failed / 4 passed open (full/half interp wrench,\n  full/resume stalls; see junit evidence).\n- DC status: direct postyield stops uz=-0.18333333333333335\n  (lambda2.66796710849, 14 accepts/26 attempts/11 cuts, min-step stop);\n  interp stops uz=-0.1135417. No fold/collapse claim: unscaled augmented\n  condition numbers are not evidence (dimensional scaling adjudication).\n- Augmented factorization already declares MatrixClass.GENERAL (D1 present\n  in product, spy regression missing). Harness v2 with active-phase\n  accounting; Astra owns timeout admission (max120 diagnostic / max600\n  pytest enforced before launch).\n\n## Completed in prior runs (evidence retained; do not repeat)\n\n- Baseline 22 + 39 passes; seven-case plastic attribution (partial-load\n  plateau decided valid); clean-HEAD VK attribution; pre-yield controls;\n  serialized Q4 checkpoint limitation documented (pre-existing).\n- Harness v2; ep_attribution.py prose; R1 corotational guard; R3 n_red==0\n  selector (corrected per supervisor recheck); R4 work_conjugate auto; R5\n  full_u(q) DC admission; tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py (16 pass).\n- EP continuation module exists with corrected reaction oracle (T1 sound);\n  T2/T3/T4 acceptance gaps open.\n\n## Reserved decisions (for Astra)\n\n- Rigid-spin equivariance contract adopted by Astra; SO(3) mean\n  applicability on the new active rotating-offset route is candidate\n  design, reviewed by Astra.\n- No physics, tolerance, success-criterion or public-contract changes made.\n", "numLines": 192, "startLine": 1, "requestedOffset": null, "requestedLimit": 2000, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": false}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "192 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\checkpoint.md", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "effect-dbcbb07e-03d5-523b-a371-f65c929aa892", "sessionId": "341d9e81-6e08-2061-eb77-520faea41e81", "turnId": "turn-542b409187d41a418292618329863619", "createdAt": 1792350094669, "updatedAt": 1792350094781, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\HANDOVER.md", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\HANDOVER.md", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\HANDOVER.md", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\HANDOVER.md", "offset": null, "limit": 2000}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\HANDOVER.md", "content": "# Handover / restart — Nonlinear master–slave beam–shell coupling (Path 1)\n\nWritten 2026-10-18 by the Antigravity agent (conversation `4a032924-ea6f-4da7-9771-04d0bdf82a44`).\nFolder: `C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/`\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Status: Slices 1–2 are done and tested. Slice 3 is partly done; acceptance is not met.**\n> Nothing is committed, pushed or reviewed. The work exists only as **uncommitted changes on `main`**\n> in `C:/Github/ANYsolver`, plus a copy in `patch/`. The \"retired and unqualified\" status of the old\n> experimental programme is unchanged: this is a new, separate attempt, not a qualification.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What this task is\n\nThe old GE/stiffened-shell nonlinear programme (archive:\n`C:/ANYworkspaceWork/beam-shell-programme-archive-20261016/`, capsule:\n`C:/Github/ANYsolver/docs/archive/beam_shell_programme/RESTART.md`) was retired in a development loop. The user picked\n**Path 1, direct nonlinear master–slave kinematic coupling**: the beam node is eliminated with an\nexact finite-rotation lever arm instead of the fixed-reference linear MPC.\n\n$$u_b = \\sum_i w_i u_{s,i} + \\big(R(\\bar\\theta_s) - I\\big)\\,r_0,\\qquad \\theta_b = \\bar\\theta_s = \\sum_i w_i\\theta_{s,i}$$\n\nThis gives the reduced residual $r_{red} = J(q)^T(F_{ext} - F_{int}(u(q)))$ and the tangent\n$K_{red} = J^T(K_T - K_{ext})J + K_{mpc,geom}$, with **zero Lagrange multipliers**. Elements use a\nwork-conjugate corotational pullback $p = B(u)^T f_{ref}(u_d)$ with an objective beam frame. That\nframe removes the objectivity obstruction found by the earlier review.\n\nThe 3-slice plan approved by the user:\n\n| Slice | Content | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | SO(3)-equivariant beam frame, exact $B(u)$, work-conjugate force and symmetric tangent, spatial moment map | **Done**, 7/7 tests |\n| 2 | Rotating-offset MPC map wired into force/displacement control, restart, reactions, postcheck | **Done**, 15/15 tests |\n| 3 | Mesh convergence R1–R4, equal-ratio and non-matching P1–P3, elastoplastic continuation, 364-test standard regression | **Partial**, see §4–§5 |\n\n## 2. Repository state (verify before doing anything)\n\n- Repo `C:/Github/ANYsolver`, branch `main`, **HEAD `b0202d335990a1fd1a647b7876ebde001aabe979`**\n  (\"fix: preserve qualified vector identity during recovery\").\n  - Someone else committed this on top of `8475718b` during the task. The work was started on\n    `8475718b`. The Slice 1/2 tests pass on the current tree, which includes `b0202d33`.\n- Modified tracked files (`git diff --shortstat`: 5 files, +1226 / −146):\n  `src/anysolver/{corotational,elements,mesh_gen,nonlinear_static,nonlinear_performance}.py`\n- Untracked new tests: `tests/test_corotational_work_conjugate.py`, `tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py`\n- Backup in `patch/` (taken 2026-10-18 19:33; SHA-256 prefixes):\n  - `slices_1_3_tracked_changes.patch`: `D62F11F4DC01A6FB` (`git diff --binary` of the 5 files against `b0202d33`)\n  - `test_corotational_work_conjugate.py`: `B5CA8D2CCB65E230`\n  - `test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py`: `21BAA1A0316D4A3C`\n- The main checkout has many unrelated dirty and untracked files from other workers. Leave them alone.\n- **Detached worktree left behind** for attribution runs:\n  `C:/Users/AudunArnesenNyhus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4a032924-ea6f-4da7-9771-04d0bdf82a44/scratch/head_wt` (at `b0202d33`).\n  Remove it with `git -C C:/Github/ANYsolver worktree remove --force <path>` once no longer needed.\n- `.development/` is **not** gitignored. This folder shows up as untracked.\n\nTo restore onto a clean checkout of `b0202d33`:\n`git apply patch/slices_1_3_tracked_changes.patch`, then copy the two test files into `tests/`.\n\n## 3. Code map (what changed where)\n\n- `corotational.py`\n  - Slice 1: `_beam_rigid_rotation` (equivariant), full-precision small-angle `rotation_matrix_from_vector` / `_rotation_right_jacobian(_inverse)` / `_rotation_left_jacobian_inverse` (Taylor terms up to $a^6$),\n    `_pullback_jacobian_factors`, `corotational_deformation_jacobian`, `spatial_moment_from_rotation_covector`,\n    `spatial_force_and_moment_resultants`, `_work_conjugate_corotational_tangent`, `corotational_work_conjugate_response`.\n  - Slice 2: `rotating_mpc_lever_arm_jacobian`, `rotating_mpc_geometric_hessian`, `NonlinearRotatingMPCEntry/Map`,\n    `has_nonlinear_rotating_mpc`, `build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map`.\n  - Slice 3 (performance only; no intended change to the mechanics):\n    - Closed-form shell frame sensitivity in `_rotation_sensitivity`, using `center_dN` now cached on\n      `_CorotationalReference`. Matches the old finite-difference version to 1e-11 relative.\n      Finite differences remain the fallback for native-frame elements (S3) and degenerate tangents.\n    - The translation columns of G are projected to zero mean, enforcing exact translation invariance.\n    - `_corotational_pullback_force_precomputed` replaces full B± rebuilds in the geometric tangent.\n    - `_fast_shell_rigid_rotation_from_tangents`.\n    - 2-node-beam translation antisymmetry shortcut. This is exact because the beam frame depends only on $x_2 - x_1$.\n- `elements.py`: `CoupledBeamShellElement.get_nonlinear_mpc_descriptor`.\n- `mesh_gen.py`: `InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement.get_nonlinear_mpc_descriptor`.\n- `nonlinear_static.py`:\n  - The rotating map is built **only when `kinematics == \"corotational\"`** (around line 5527).\n  - It is threaded through force control, displacement control, restart, reactions and `constraint_postcheck`.\n  - `auto` tangent resolves to `work_conjugate` for coupled models.\n- `nonlinear_performance.py`: `_solve_static_displacement_control_block` forwards `rotating_mpc_map`.\n\n## 4. Evidence gathered\n\n**Tests (last run 2026-10-18 08:23, after all Slice 3 code changes):**\n\n- `pytest tests/test_corotational_work_conjugate.py tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py -q`\n  → **22 passed** (52.9 s). Before the Slice 3 performance work this took about 175 s.\n- `tests/test_standard_edge_beam_shell_transfer.py` + `tests/test_standard_edge_beam_shell_nonlinear_contact.py`\n  → 39 passed. This run was on 2026-10-17, **before** the Slice 3 performance changes, and is **not re-run since**.\n\n**Convergence data** (reproduce with `diagnostics/convergence_study.py`). Setup: cantilever strip\n1.0 × 0.24 × 0.012 m, 10 × 40 mm stiffener at e = 0.04 m, beam-tip uz in m.\n\n| Linear, 12 kN | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R (n_beam = nx/2) | −0.039080 | −0.033271 | −0.030669 | −0.029967 | −0.029774 |\n| M (n_beam = nx) | −0.028828 | −0.029381 | −0.029550 | −0.029620 | −0.029654 |\n| P (n_beam = 1.5 nx) | −0.028718 | −0.028850 | −0.029334 | – | – |\n\n- R and M converge to the same limit (about −0.0297).\n- R converges slowly from above, so half-density beams are a poor discretisation.\n- P converges, but tip rotation at P3 is still 0.8% below M5.\n\n**Nonlinear corotational runs:**\n\n- At 12 kN (about 2.5° tip rotation), R1–R3 give −0.039990 / −0.033679 / −0.030821. Each stays\n  within ≤ 2.3% of the matching linear value, and the gap shrinks with refinement.\n  - Run time for R1/R2/R3 dropped from 7.2 / 21.2 / 54.1 s to 2.7 / 5.8 / 13.1 s.\n- At 140 kN (about 28°):\n\n  | Mesh | uz | Tip rotation |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | M1 | −0.308331 | 27.03° |\n  | M2 | −0.333367 | 28.63° |\n  | M3 | −0.329180 | 28.13° |\n  | P1 | −0.340495 | 29.08° |\n  | P2 | −0.321265 | 27.59° |\n  | P3 | −0.329432 | 28.13° |\n\n  - M3 and P3 agree to 0.08% in uz, so matching and non-matching couplings converge together.\n  - All runs converged.\n  - **There is no independent reference solution.** This shows self-consistency only, not accuracy.\n\n**Elastoplastic investigation** (`diagnostics/ep_isolation.py`, `diagnostics/ep_sweep.py`):\n\n1. An apparent \"plastic stiffer than elastic\" result was **caused by my own inconsistent ad-hoc\n   DNV-C208 curve**: the power-law branch jumped to about 225 MPa above a 130 MPa plateau.\n   - With the repository curve `dnv_c208_steel_curve(\"S355\", 0.012)`, beam-only and shell-only\n     von Kármán runs soften correctly.\n   - Always use repository curves.\n2. Beam-only and shell-only **corotational + plastic** runs fail: the fiber return map does not\n   converge, and a shell Jacobian degenerates.\n   - **This is identical on clean HEAD** (worktree run), so it is pre-existing and not caused by Slices 1–3.\n   - Those loads were also 1.75–4× the plastic collapse moment, so the runs were ill-posed under force control.\n3. Coupled sweep, S355, 6 steps (uz at the shell tip node; elastic control = curve stresses × 1e4):\n\n| Fz/node | VK elastic | VK plastic (α_max) | CR elastic | CR plastic (α_max) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| −2 000 | −0.01089 | −0.01089 (0) | −0.01106 | −0.01106 (0) |\n| −6 000 | **+0.00431** | −0.01675 (3.4e-4) | −0.03315 | **−0.17746 (2.3e-2)** |\n| −10 000 | −0.01689 | −0.01669 (3.4e-4) | −0.05515 | **−0.17687 (2.3e-2)** |\n| −14 000 | −0.08309 | −0.01671 (3.4e-4) | −0.07702 | **−0.17713 (2.3e-2)** |\n\n- **Pass:**\n  - Before yield, EP equals elastic exactly.\n  - At small rotation, corotational and von Kármán agree within 1.6%.\n  - Corotational elastic response is close to linear in load.\n- **Red: unexplained, do not ignore.**\n  - **Corotational plastic gives nearly the same uz (about −0.177) and α_max (about 0.0228) for every load from 6 to 35 kN per node.**\n    A solution that doesn't depend on the load points to the reported state not being the\n    equilibrium at load factor 1. Candidates: the load factor actually reached, early termination\n    reported as converged, a state/commit mix-up, or a mechanism plateau.\n  - Von Kármán coupled runs are also inconsistent: the elastic run is non-monotonic and changes\n    sign, and the plastic run doesn't depend on load either.\n  - The von Kármán path does **not** use the new rotating map, so at least that part is probably\n    pre-existing, but this was **not verified on HEAD**.\n\n## 5. Slice 3 acceptance status\n\n| Criterion | Status |\n|---|---|\n| R1–R3 nonlinear runs converge and track linear | Met (no independent reference) |\n| **R4 (32×8/16) nonlinear** | **Not run** (expected about 30–40 s now) |\n| Equal-ratio and non-matching P1–P3 converge to a common limit | Met at the linear level and at about 28° (self-consistency) |\n| **Elastoplastic continuation on the coupled model** | **Not met.** Red finding in §4.3 |\n| **Full 364-test / 25-module standard beam–shell regression** | **Not run.** Only 39 tests from 2 modules ran, and before the performance changes |\n| Independent reference, e.g. a published stiffened-panel or cantilever large-rotation benchmark | **Not done** |\n| Review | **Not reviewed** (self-checks only) |\n\n## 6. Recommended next actions (in order)\n\n1. **Re-verify the baseline.**\n   - Confirm HEAD and the patch hash, then re-run the 22 Slice 1/2 tests.\n   - Re-run the two standard-edge modules (39 tests), which now go through the Slice 3 performance code.\n2. **Resolve the §4.3 red finding first.** It decides whether the elastoplastic part of Path 1 is usable.\n   - Question: does the coupled plastic solve actually reach load factor 1 at equilibrium?\n   - Experiment: for Fz = −6k / −10k / −14k, print the final load factor, accepted increment\n     history, cutbacks and final reduced residual from the result object. Also evaluate\n     $\\|r_{red}\\|$ independently at the returned state using `_assemble_nonlinear_system` +\n     `mpc_map.reduce_force`.\n   - Repeat the coupled von Kármán case on the `head_wt` worktree to attribute it.\n   - Decision rules:\n     - **λ < 1, or a large independent residual:** it's a solver/reporting bug. Find out whether\n       the rotating-MPC path (the state passed to `apply_kinematics` vs the committed state) or\n       pre-existing code is responsible.\n     - **λ = 1 and the residual is small:** check whether the load exceeds coupled collapse. Use\n       loads below the elastic–plastic limit, or switch to displacement control.\n3. Run R4 and the full standard regression (25 modules).\n4. Only then: an independent reference benchmark, and review.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Retry limit (`C:/Github/AGENTS.md`): the elastoplastic question has taken three exploratory\n> passes (ad-hoc curve, S355 isolation, sweep). The next pass should be the bounded experiment in\n> step 2, not more open-ended exploration. If that doesn't decide it, report back to the owner.\n\n## 7. Restart prompt (paste into a fresh session)\n\n> Continue the nonlinear master–slave beam–shell coupling task (Path 1). First read\n> `C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/HANDOVER.md`.\n> Then verify the repo state in §2: HEAD `b0202d33`, the 5 modified files, the 2 untracked tests,\n> and the patch hash `D62F11F4DC01A6FB`. Do not commit, push or touch unrelated dirty files.\n> Execute §6 steps 1–2 only, then report using the completion checklist from `C:/Github/AGENTS.md`.\n\n## 8. Active Slice 3 implementation — 2026-10-18\n\nThe user explicitly authorized implementation of the complete five-part Slice 3\nplan in the current Codex chat. This supersedes the narrow restart prompt above.\nPolicy remains ANY_ECOSYSTEM_RISK_PROPORTIONATE_ENGINEERING_V1, revision\n2026-09-24.2. Preserve scientific criteria, historical failures and retirement;\nno old programme execution allowance is reused. No commit, push or release.\n\nResume inspection confirmed HEAD b0202d33, the five-file +1226/-146 diff and\nboth test hashes in §2. The current patch equals the backup after normalizing\nUTF-8 BOM and CRLF. `converged` also means `stopped_at_limit` on clean HEAD;\ntherefore a partial load is not by itself a solver defect. Status, achieved\nload and independently reconstructed residual must distinguish the cases.\n\nAuthorized outcome: baseline checks; the bounded plastic attribution batch;\ndirect/interpolated S355 pre-yield, displacement continuation to -0.20 m,\nsplit restart at -0.10 m and trial/cancellation integrity; R1–R4 small-load\nand M1–M4/P1–P4 finite-load convergence; independently reviewed analytical\ncoupled bending; exact historical 25-module regression plus new modules;\nnon-author review and evidence-based acceptance. Public `converged` semantics\nand all existing tolerances remain compatible.\n\nNew numerical allowance: 3600 process-wall seconds cumulative for this Slice 3\nimplementation, all attempts counted, with 900 seconds reserved for final\nverification. Individual diagnostic timeout 120 seconds; regression timeout\n600 seconds. One numerical child at a time within this task. Record commands,\nsource/input identities, effective runtime, full stdout/stderr, exit/timeout,\nprecise process-wall and budget consumed/rema