product/EP workflow (SLICE3_PRODUCT_DELIVERY.md,60turns,final12reserved). No new\nallowance. Astra owns the independent analytical and mesh acceptance executables\nconcurrently: this keeps scientific applicability/resource integration with the\nacceptance owner and makes oracle authorship independent of the product author;\nMistral retains central product mechanics, connected integration and EP delivery.\nParent launches no numerical child until this focused worker hands back.\n\nThird worker run reached60-turn bound without handoff. Actual artifacts show\n16 source-regression passes (slice3-repairs-5), then7failed/4passed EP cases\n(slice3-continuation-1). Original-grid DC stops at maximum_iterations_reached,\ndirect uz=-1/6m and interpolated uz=-1/12m; accepted states have positive\nplasticity. These are incomplete continuation results, not collapse evidence.\nThe owner continues narrowly on DC/state/test repair via supervisor_findings.md\ndelta (60turns,final12reserved). No execution allowance renewal. A manual\nGENERAL-matrix probe still stalls at the next direct increment, so symmetric\nmatrix classification alone does not explain this fixture's failure. Independent\nreview separately confirmed that classification is a real backend defect.\nAt probe completion26 attempts cost974.5599942000408s;2625.440005799959s remain,\nincluding900s final reserve. Root numerical execution remains suspended while\nthe owner edits/runs product checks. Independent mesh/arc oracles and exact final\nselection runners are implemented but have not yet executed any FE assessment.\n\nFourth worker run reached its60-turn bound without final handoff. Actual source\nadds GENERAL augmented factorization and adaptive failed-control subdivision.\nThe direct route reaches-.18333333333333335m (14accepted,26attempts), interpolated\n-.11354166666666668m (10accepted,21attempts), then minimum-control-step stop.\nBoth remain incomplete against-.20m. Independent review found zero-span retries\ncan be unbounded and per-record iterations double-counted; these are actionable\nrepair findings, not accepted candidate behavior. A half-run subset gives5passes,\n1failure,5deselected: interpolated-.10m support wrench imbalance12.8765269 versus\n61917.1985 applied scale (required1e-6 relative), despite reduced equilibrium.\nThe dimensional augmented SVD condition number does not prove a physical fold;\nthat worker interpretation is not adopted. ResidualFD sign explains≈2 in probes.\n\n31 attempts now cost1486.0224586999684s, leaving2113.9775413000316s including900\nfinal reserve. Two diagnostic attempts requested180s but completed88.7512515s/\n112.9044385s; preserve the timeout-admission discrepancy. Astra now owns harness\ntimeout admission, enforcing120 diagnostics/600 regression before launch.\nSame Mistral owner receives SLICE3_UNBLOCK_DELIVERY.md,80turns, early checkpoint12,\nhandoff by60/final15reserved, maximum450 additional numerical seconds. Objective\nrigid-spin-equivariant interpolation is adopted as a physical contract; an SO(3)\nmean is a candidate if a discriminating check confirms the averaging defect.\nNo material, tolerance, API or success-definition changes are authorized. Full\nhistory/snapshot and zero-span findings must be closed. Mesh/arc/final checks\nremain for independent assessment after a stable candidate. No allowance renewal.\n", "numLines": 305, "startLine": 1, "requestedOffset": null, "requestedLimit": 2000, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": false}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "305 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\HANDOVER.md", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
