{"id": "reasoning-0a8885dc-9b49-55fe-9d46-58aa3163c39b-0", "sessionId": "341d9e81-6e08-2061-eb77-520faea41e81", "turnId": "turn-542b409187d41a418292618329863619", "createdAt": 1792350235149, "updatedAt": 1792350235149, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "The weight validator admits mixed-sign weights (partition of unity). Per adoption: refuse negative weights on the active mean route with explicit ValueError. I'll enforce in `_so3_weighted_mean` (or at map build time — better at build time so it fails closed early, before constitutive activation). Actually both: build-time check in `build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map` for multi-master entries with any negative weight → ValueError. Single-master direct has w=1 always.\n\nNow let me write the implementation. Plan for corotational.py edits:\n\nA. Add `_so3_weighted_mean(master_thetas, weights, label)` after `_nonlinear_minus_linear_rotation` / near rotating_mpc functions. Returns (theta_m, G_tuple).\n\nB. Modify `NonlinearRotatingMPCEntry.__init__` to accept `master_theta_projs` and store; add `weights` property; add method `mean_and_tangents(u)` returning (theta_lin, theta_m, G_list).\n\nC. Rewrite map methods: apply_kinematics, to_linear_displacement, jacobian, reduce_force, geometric_tangent, transfer_slave_imbalance_to_masters.\n\nD. build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map: compute per-master theta projections; negative-weight refusal; extend downstream guard to multi-master slave rotations.\n\nE. Extend `_reject_downstream_rotating_slave_translation_dependencies` → also rotations of multi-master entries.\n\nLet me now check how `jacobian`'s existing structure builds blocks so my rewrite is consistent, and check where else `entry.theta_proj` is used outside corotational.py:", "summary": []}
