_objectivity_review.md exact moment-defect discriminator and complete acceptance tests. ... Continue DC globalization/state/restart and all accepted snapshot/history coverage; source/test changes from previous run are unverified.\"\n\nSo priorities: (1) wrapper fix [done], (2) SO3 mean + connected seams, (3) discriminator + acceptance tests, (4) continue DC globalization/state/restart + snapshot/history coverage (the T2/T3/T4 closures — many already in the test file per what I see: every-snapshot reconstruction is already implemented in _assert_completed_dc_case). The checkpoint said intended edits include DC line search, lambda recovery (done in nonlinear_static + now forwarded), D1 spy regression, zero-span regression, T2/T3/T4 closures. Some of these may already be implemented from the previous run (\"source/test changes from previous run are unverified\"). Let me check what's already in the source from the previous run: DC line search? Let me grep nonlinear_static for line search.\n\nGiven the budget and turn limits (Max160, candidate by 20, handoff by 120, final 40), I should focus: the mean implementation is the core. Then verify with cheap map tests + the interp half case. DC globalization (line search) — check if already present; if present, it's unverified; the half/full runs will exercise it.\n\nLet me check for the line search in nonlinear_static.", "summary": []}
