{"id": "reasoning-49b44052-d621-5c58-b282-2031be2a01aa-0", "sessionId": "341d9e81-6e08-2061-eb77-520faea41e81", "turnId": "turn-542b409187d41a418292618329863619", "createdAt": 1792350269343, "updatedAt": 1792350269343, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "There's a general line-search framework in the load-increment settings, but the checkpoint's intended edit #1 was a \"DC bounded residual line search on the adaptive rotating-MPC route\" — let me check whether the previous run implemented it in the DC solver. Grep for the DC-specific globalization near the DC Newton loop. Let me search for \"_dc\" line search or \"residual line search\" markers.", "summary": []}
