{"id": "reasoning-268da9a3-71f8-525d-b619-9e5c6f9f3a21-0", "sessionId": "341d9e81-6e08-2061-eb77-520faea41e81", "turnId": "turn-542b409187d41a418292618329863619", "createdAt": 1792350290793, "updatedAt": 1792350290793, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "The file ends at line 1552 with the builder. So the region from 1238 (`class NonlinearRotatingMPCEntry`) to end of file is what I'm rewriting, plus inserting `_so3_weighted_mean` before `rotating_mpc_lever_arm_jacobian` (line 1195).\n\nLet me now write the new code. I'll construct the replacement text carefully.\n\nKey design decisions recap:\n- `_so3_weighted_mean(master_thetas, weights, label)` → (theta_m, G_tuple). Refusals: negative weights, partition-of-unity, non-convergence, chart boundary (||psi_i|| >= pi*(1-1e-6)), singular B.\n- Entry: add `master_theta_projs` param; add `mean_state(u)`; keep `master_rotation` (theta_lin).\n- Map methods rewritten as derived.\n- Guard extended to multi-master slave rotations; renamed.\n- Builder: computes master_theta_projs; refuses negative weights on multi-master entries.\n\nOne important check — `spatial_moment_from_rotation_covector(theta, covector)` uses J_l(theta)^{-T}. In the transfer, master rotation covectors G_i^T v are additive rotation covectors at master theta_i. The reaction oracle converts them with J_l(theta_i)^{-T}. The wrench-preservation identity: sum_i J_l(theta_i)^{-T} G_i^T v should equal J_l(theta_m)^{-T} v (spatial moment of the slave wrench at the mean orientation, plus lever arm...). That's exactly the identity sum_i G_i J_l(theta_i)^{-1} = J_l(theta_m)^{-1} transposed. ✓ consistent with the review.\n\nNow write the code. Note the file uses CRLF; my Python replacement script will handle that by writing with newline=''.\n\nLet me write the new sections:\n\n```python\ndef _so3_weighted_mean(\n    master_thetas: Sequence[np.ndarray],\n    weights: Sequence[float],\n    label: str,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, Tuple[np.ndarray, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"Intrinsic weighted SO(3) mean with exact tangent derivatives.\n\n    Returns ``(theta_m, (G_i, ...))`` where ``R(theta_m)`` solves the\n    Karcher-type condition ``sum_i w_i Log(R_m^T R_i) = 0`` and\n    ``G_i = dtheta_m/dtheta_i`` is its exact differential:\n\n        G_i = R_m B^{-1} w_i J_l(psi_i)^{-1} R_m^T,\n        B   = sum_i w_i J_l(psi_i)^{-1},  psi_i = Log(R_m^T R_i).\n\n    The mean is left-equivariant: for a common superposed rotation ``Q``,\n    ``mean(Q R_i) = Q mean(R_i)``, and the tangents satisfy the differential\n    rigid-spin identity ``sum_i G_i J_l(theta_i)^{-1} = J_l(theta_m)^{-1}``.\n\n    Refusal boundary (adopted contract): weights must be nonnegative and form\n    a partition of unity; the fixed-point iteration must converge from the\n    linear average with every master inside the principal chart of the mean\n    (``|psi_i| < pi``), and ``B`` must stay nonsingular.  Ambiguous, chart\n    crossing and singular cases are refused explicitly instead of silently\n    selecting a branch.  A single master and exactly identical master\n    rotations are exact short-circuits.\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nImplementation details:\n- max iterations 100, tol 1e-14 on ||f||.\n- Also guard: if ||f|| grows > pi during iteration → refuse early.\n\nNow the entry:\n\n```python\nclass NonlinearRotatingMPCEntry:\n    def __init__(self, *, element_id, slave_u_dofs, slave_theta_dofs, masters,\n                 eccentricity, theta_proj, label_prefix, master_theta_projs=()):\n        ...\n        self.master_theta_projs = tuple(\n            sparse.csr_matrix(p, dtype=float) for p in master_theta_projs\n        )  # need scipy import — the module imports? check top of file\n```\n\nCheck imports at top of corotational.py — does it import scipy.sparse at module level? The map's __init__ does `from scipy import sparse` locally. I'll do the same locally or check module imports. Let me check the header quickly. Actually the entry __init__ currently uses `.tocsr()` on theta_proj — theta_proj passed already as csr from builder. I'll pass master_theta_projs as csr from the builder and just tuple() them.\n\nEntry methods:\n\n```python\n    def master_rotations(self, u: np.ndarray) -> list:\n        return [np.asarray(u[m_theta], dtype=float).reshape(3) for _m_u, m_theta, _w in self.masters]\n\n    def mean_state(self, u: np.ndarray):\n        thetas = self.master_rotations(u)\n        weights = [w for _m_u, _m_theta, w in self.masters]\n        return _so3_weighted_mean(thetas, weights, self.label_prefix)\n```\n\nMap methods (full rewrite):\n\napply_kinematics:\n```python\n    def apply_kinematics(self, u_linear: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        \"\"\"Map a linear MPC displacement state ``u_lin`` to the nonlinear manifold.\"\"\"\n        u = np.asarray(u_linear, dtype=float).reshape(-1).copy()\n        if not self.entries:\n            return u\n        corrections = []\n        for entry in self.entries:\n            theta_lin = entry.master_rotation(u)\n            theta_m, _G = entry.mean_state(u)\n            d_theta = theta_m - theta_lin\n            delta_u = _nonlinear_minus_linear_rotation(theta_m) @ entry.eccentricity\n            delta_u = delta_u + np.cross(d_theta, entry.eccentricity)\n            corrections.append((entry, d_theta, delta_u))\n        for entry, d_theta, delta_u in corrections:\n            u[entry.slave_u_dofs] += delta_u\n            u[entry.slave_theta_dofs] += d_theta\n        return u\n```\n\nWait — np.cross(d_theta, r_0) = skew(d_theta) r_0. And I derived correction = _nonlinear_minus_linear_rotation(theta_m) @ r_0 + skew(theta_m - theta_lin) @ r_0. ✓\n\nto_linear_displacement:\n```python\n        u_lin = copy\n        corrections = same computed from u_lin (input)\n        for entry, d_theta, delta_u in corrections:\n            u_lin[entry.slave_u_dofs] -= delta_u\n            u_lin[entry.slave_theta_dofs] -= d_theta\n        return u_lin\n```\n\njacobian:\n```python\n    def jacobian(self, u_current):\n        from scipy import sparse\n        if not self.entries:\n            return self.T_linear\n        u = ...\n        row_blocks, col_blocks, data_blocks = [], [], []\n        for entry in self.entries:\n            if entry.theta_proj.nnz == 0 and all(p.nnz == 0 for p in entry.master_theta_projs):\n                continue\n            theta_m, G_list = entry.mean_state(u)\n            A = rotating_mpc_lever_arm_jacobian(theta_m, entry.eccentricity)\n            # M_proj = sum_i G_i P_i\n            M = None\n            for G, P in zip(G_list, entry.master_theta_projs):\n                if P.nnz == 0:\n                    continue\n                term = sparse.csr_matrix(G) @ P\n                M = term if M is None else M + term\n            if M is None:\n                continue\n            C_u = sparse.csr_matrix(A) @ M + sparse.csr_matrix(entry.r_skew) @ entry.theta_proj\n            C_theta = M - entry.theta_proj\n            for rows, block in ((entry.slave_u_dofs, C_u), (entry.slave_theta_dofs, C_theta)):\n                coo = block.tocoo()\n                if coo.nnz:\n                    row_blocks.append(np.asarray(rows)[coo.row])\n                    col_blocks.append(coo.col)\n                    data_blocks.append(coo.data)\n        ...same assembly...\n```\n\nHmm wait — for direct entries: M = G P = P = theta_proj; C_u = A theta_proj + skew(r_0) theta_proj = delta_A theta_proj ✓; C_theta = 0 → no block. ✓ identical to old.\n\nEdge: entry.theta_proj.nnz==0 but master projs nonzero? theta_proj = sum w P; if all P nnz==0 then theta_proj nnz==0. If theta_proj nnz==0, C_u = A M (M could be nonzero? no — theta_proj = sum w_i P_i = 0 pattern-wise... could cancel? patterns with mixed signs... skip this edge; the check `if coo.nnz` handles it).\n\nActually simpler: don't skip; just compute. The old code checked nothing except building. Keep it simple: compute per entry; blocks with no nnz skipped naturally.