{"id": "effect-f34f92d7-f25a-56ec-8109-20a3dec523ef", "sessionId": "341d9e81-6e08-2061-eb77-520faea41e81", "turnId": "turn-542b409187d41a418292618329863619", "createdAt": 1792350307810, "updatedAt": 1792350307845, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.write_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.write_file", "display": {"summary": "Writing C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\patch\\_so3_mean_block.py", "content": "def _so3_weighted_mean(\n    master_thetas,\n    weights,\n    label,\n):\n    # -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n    \"\"\"Intrinsic weighted SO(3) mean with exact tangent derivatives.\n\n    Returns ``(theta_m, (G_i, ...))`` where ``R(theta_m)`` solves the\n    Karcher-type condition ``sum_i w_i Log(R_m^T R_i) = 0`` and\n    ``G_i = dtheta_m/dtheta_i`` is its exact differential:\n\n        G_i = R_m B^{-1} w_i J_l(psi_i)^{-1} R_m^T,\n        B   = sum_i w_i J_l(psi_i)^{-1},   psi_i = Log(R_m^T R_i).\n\n    The mean is left-equivariant: for a common superposed rotation ``Q``,\n    ``mean(Q R_i, w) = Q mean(R_i, w)``, and the tangents satisfy the\n    differential rigid-spin identity\n    ``sum_i G_i J_l(theta_i)^{-1} = J_l(theta_m)^{-1}``, which is the\n    covector-transfer counterpart of physical wrench preservation.\n\n    Refusal boundary (adopted contract): weights must be nonnegative and\n    form a partition of unity; the fixed-point iteration must converge from\n    the linear average with every master inside the principal chart of the\n    mean (``|psi_i| < pi``), and ``B`` must remain nonsingular.  Ambiguous,\n    chart-crossing and singular cases are refused explicitly instead of\n    silently selecting a branch.  A single master and exactly identical\n    master rotations are exact short-circuits, so the direct route and the\n    identical-rotation limit reproduce the legacy map bit-for-bit.\n    \"\"\"\n    thetas = [np.asarray(t, dtype=float).reshape(3).copy() for t in master_thetas]\n    ws = [float(w) for w in weights]\n    if not thetas:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{label}: SO(3) mean requires at least one master\")\n    if any(w < 0.0 for w in ws):\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{label}: the intrinsic SO(3) mean on the active rotating-offset \"\n            f\"route requires nonnegative weights; got {ws}\"\n        )\n    weight_sum = float(sum(ws))\n    if abs(weight_sum - 1.0) > 1.0e-8:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{label}: the intrinsic SO(3) mean requires weights forming a \"\n            f\"partition of unity; got sum {weight_sum!r}\"\n        )\n    if len(thetas) == 1:\n        return thetas[0], (np.eye(3),)\n    first = thetas[0]\n    if all(np.array_equal(t, first) for t in thetas[1:]):\n        return first.copy(), tuple(w * np.eye(3) for w in ws)\n\n    theta_m = np.zeros(3, dtype=float)\n    for t, w in zip(thetas, ws):\n        theta_m += w * t\n    R_m = rotation_matrix_from_vector(theta_m)\n    psis = []\n    converged = False\n    for _ in range(100):\n        psis = [\n            rotation_vector_from_matrix(R_m.T @ rotation_matrix_from_vector(t))\n            for t in thetas\n        ]\n        f = np.zeros(3, dtype=float)\n        for psi, w in zip(psis, ws):\n            f += w * psi\n        if float(np.linalg.norm(f)) <= 1.0e-14:\n            converged = True\n            break\n        if float(np.linalg.norm(f)) >= np.pi:\n            break\n        R_m = R_m @ rotation_matrix_from_vector(f)\n    if not converged:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{label}: intrinsic SO(3) mean did not converge in the local \"\n            \"convex neighborhood; the master rotations are ambiguous or \"\n            \"outside the supported chart\"\n        )\n    for psi in psis:\n        if float(np.linalg.norm(psi)) >= float(np.pi) * (1.0 - 1.0e-6):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"{label}: intrinsic SO(3) mean lies on the chart boundary \"\n                f\"to a master (|psi|={float(np.linalg.norm(psi))}); \"\n                \"ambiguous mean refused\"\n            )\n    A = [_rotation_left_jacobian_inverse(psi) for psi in psis]\n    B = np.zeros((3, 3), dtype=float)\n    for a, w in zip(A, ws):\n        B += w * a\n    if abs(float(np.linalg.det(B))) <= 1.0e-10:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{label}: intrinsic SO(3) mean tangent operator is singular; \"\n            \"ambiguous mean refused\"\n        )\n    B_inv = np.linalg.inv(B)\n    G = []\n    for a, w in zip(A, ws):\n        G.append(R_m @ (B_inv @ (w * a)) @ R_m.T)\n    theta_m = rotation_vector_from_matrix(R_m)\n    return theta_m, tuple(G)\n", "suffix": "", "verb": "Creating", "message": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\patch\\_so3_mean_block.py", "settledVerb": "Created", "settledMessage": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\patch\\_so3_mean_block.py", "statusText": "Writing file"}, "kind": "file_write", "input": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\patch\\_so3_mean_block.py", "content": "def _so3_weighted_mean(\n    master_thetas,\n    weights,\n    label,\n):\n    # -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n    \"\"\"Intrinsic weighted SO(3) mean with exact tangent derivatives.\n\n    Returns ``(theta_m, (G_i, ...))`` where ``R(theta_m)`` solves the\n    Karcher-type condition ``sum_i w_i Log(R_m^T R_i) = 0`` and\n    ``G_i = dtheta_m/dtheta_i`` is its exact differential:\n\n        G_i = R_m B^{-1} w_i J_l(psi_i)^{-1} R_m^T,\n        B   = sum_i w_i J_l(psi_i)^{-1},   psi_i = Log(R_m^T R_i).\n\n    The mean is left-equivariant: for a common superposed rotation ``Q``,\n    ``mean(Q R_i, w) = Q mean(R_i, w)``, and the tangents satisfy the\n    differential rigid-spin identity\n    ``sum_i G_i J_l(theta_i)^{-1} = J_l(theta_m)^{-1}``, which is the\n    covector-transfer counterpart of physical wrench preservation.\n\n    Refusal boundary (adopted contract): weights must be nonnegative and\n    form a partition of unity; the fixed-point iteration must converge from\n    the linear average with every master inside the principal chart of the\n    mean (``|psi_i| < pi``), and ``B`` must remain nonsingular.  Ambiguous,\n    chart-crossing and singular cases are refused explicitly instead of\n    silently selecting a branch.  A single master and exactly identical\n    master rotations are exact short-circuits, so the direct route and the\n    identical-rotation limit reproduce the legacy map bit-for-bit.\n    \"\"\"\n    thetas = [np.asarray(t, dtype=float).reshape(3).copy() for t in master_thetas]\n    ws = [float(w) for w in weights]\n    if not thetas:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{label}: SO(3) mean requires at least one master\")\n    if any(w < 0.0 for w in ws):\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{label}: the intrinsic SO(3) mean on the active rotating-offset \"\n            f\"route requires nonnegative weights; got {ws}\"\n        )\n    weight_sum = float(sum(ws))\n    if abs(weight_sum - 1.0) > 1.0e-8:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{label}: the intrinsic SO(3) mean requires weights forming a \"\n            f\"partition of unity; got sum {weight_sum!r}\"\n        )\n    if len(thetas) == 1:\n        return thetas[0], (np.eye(3),)\n    first = thetas[0]\n    if all(np.array_equal(t, first) for t in thetas[1:]):\n        return first.copy(), tuple(w * np.eye(3) for w in ws)\n\n    theta_m = np.zeros(3, dtype=float)\n    for t, w in zip(thetas, ws):\n        theta_m += w * t\n    R_m = rotation_matrix_from_vector(theta_m)\n    psis = []\n    converged = False\n    for _ in range(100):\n        psis = [\n            rotation_vector_from_matrix(R_m.T @ rotation_matrix_from_vector(t))\n            for t in thetas\n        ]\n        f = np.zeros(3, dtype=float)\n        for psi, w in zip(psis, ws):\n            f += w * psi\n        if float(np.linalg.norm(f)) <= 1.0e-14:\n            converged = True\n            break\n        if float(np.linalg.norm(f)) >= np.pi:\n            break\n        R_m = R_m @ rotation_matrix_from_vector(f)\n    if not converged:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{label}: intrinsic SO(3) mean did not converge in the local \"\n            \"convex neighborhood; the master rotations are ambiguous or \"\n            \"outside the supported chart\"\n        )\n    for psi in psis:\n        if float(np.linalg.norm(psi)) >= float(np.pi) * (1.0 - 1.0e-6):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"{label}: intrinsic SO(3) mean lies on the chart boundary \"\n                f\"to a master (|psi|={float(np.linalg.norm(psi))}); \"\n                \"ambiguous mean refused\"\n            )\n    A = [_rotation_left_jacobian_inverse(psi) for psi in psis]\n    B = np.zeros((3, 3), dtype=float)\n    for a, w in zip(A, ws):\n        B += w * a\n    if abs(float(np.linalg.det(B))) <= 1.0e-10:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{label}: intrinsic SO(3) mean tangent operator is singular; \"\n            \"ambiguous mean refused\"\n        )\n    B_inv = np.linalg.inv(B)\n    G = []\n    for a, w in zip(A, ws):\n        G.append(R_m @ (B_inv @ (w * a)) @ R_m.T)\n    theta_m = rotation_vector_from_matrix(R_m)\n    return theta_m, tuple(G)\n"}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\patch\\_so3_mean_block.py", "content": "def _so3_weighted_mean(\n    master_thetas,\n    weights,\n    label,\n):\n    # -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n    \"\"\"Intrinsic weighted SO(3) mean with exact tangent derivatives.\n\n    Returns ``(theta_m, (G_i, ...))`` where ``R(theta_m)`` solves the\n    Karcher-type condition ``sum_i w_i Log(R_m^T R_i) = 0`` and\n    ``G_i = dtheta_m/dtheta_i`` is its exact differential:\n\n        G_i = R_m B^{-1} w_i J_l(psi_i)^{-1} R_m^T,\n        B   = sum_i w_i J_l(psi_i)