lin → d_theta = 0 → d_u = _nmlr(theta_lin) @ r_0 = old delta_R @ r_0. ✓\n\nNow — one more critical check on `jacobian` for the DIRECT case: C_u = A @ M + S @ theta_proj with M = P_1 = theta_proj → (A + S) theta_proj = delta_A theta_proj ✓. C_theta = M - theta_proj = 0 → skipped by np.any check. ✓ identical to old.\n\nNow, about `geometric_tangent` for the direct case: covectors(thetas) with single master: mean short-circuit G=I → cov = A(theta_m)^T f_b + m_b with theta_m = theta_1. D[0][0] = d(A^T f_b)/dtheta_1 = old H_b. ✓ (m_b constant drops). The old code symmetrized H_b; new symmetrizes the total. ✓\n\nOne issue in geometric_tangent: `covectors` closure captures f_b, m_b — fine. But `_so3_weighted_mean` with perturbed thetas: the identical-rotation short-circuit uses np.array_equal — with perturbed thetas not all equal → iteration. Fine.\n\nFD step h=1e-6 on thetas: thetas can be large (e.g. 0.5 rad); relative perturbation fine.\n\nNow — `reduce_force` for entries where theta_proj/... no skip needed.\n\nOne more thing: `jacobian` — old code note: for entries where `entry.theta_proj.nnz == 0` but master projs nonzero — my skip condition `if entry.theta_proj.nnz == 0 and all(p.nnz == 0...)` — if theta_proj is zero but master projs nonzero (possible? theta_proj = sum w P_i; if weights zero... weights are nonzero by descriptor filter). Keep as is.\n\nNow, also `NonlinearRotatingMPCEntry.__init__` signature changed (added master_theta_projs with default ()). Any other construction sites? Only the builder. ✓\n\n`master_translation` retained (used anywhere? grep showed only within corotational? It was in the old code; keep).\n\nNow splice into corotational.py:\n1. Insert `_so3_mean_block.py` content before `def rotating_mpc_lever_arm_jacobian(`.\n2. Replace from `class NonlinearRotatingMPCEntry:` to EOF with `_map_block.py` content.\n\nThe blocks I wrote use LF; the file uses CRLF. I'll normalize the inserted text to CRLF when writing. Also the blocks contain `# -*- co