gned with entries? Entries are built in element-id order; couplings in construction order — same order (mpc ids 200+ix in order). Safer: build a dof→position map from all nodes: for each node, dofs = get_node_dofs(nid); position X. Then for any translation dof, position lookup.\n\n```python\n    dofmap = {}\n    for node in model.mesh.nodes.values():\n        dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(node.node_id)  # check API\n        X = np.array([node.x, node.y, node.z])\n        for d in dofs[:3]:\n            dofmap[int(d)] = X\n```\nNeed node iteration API — model.mesh.nodes? In the builder they use model.mesh.get_node(id) with .x/.y/.z attributes. And node ids: shell grid 1..(nx+1)(ny+1), beam 100+. I can iterate meta: masters from couplings + slave nodes. Simpler: collect from meta[\"couplings\"]: for each coupling: masters (node ids), slave (node id). Positions via model.mesh.get_node.\n\nThen spun state:\n```python\n    for coupling in meta[\"couplings\"]:\n        for nid in coupling[\"masters\"]:\n            dofs = get_node_dofs(nid)\n            X = pos(nid)\n            u_lin_spun[dofs[:3]] = (Q - I) @ X + Q @ u_lin[dofs[:3]]\n            u_lin_spun[dofs[3:6]] = rotation_vector_from_matrix(Q @ rotation_matrix_from_vector(u_lin[dofs[3:6]]))\n```\nNote: spinning the LINEAR state's master dofs; slave dofs of u_lin (linear MPC values) will be recomputed by apply_kinematics — but apply_kinematics only corrects slave dofs; the slave dofs in u_lin_spun retain linear values from... the linear constraint says u_b,lin = sum w u_i + theta_lin × r_0. If I spin only masters and leave slave linear entries stale, apply adds corrections to the stale values — wrong. I must set the slave linear entries consistently: u_lin_spun[slave_u] = sum w u_i' + theta_lin' × r_0 and slave theta = theta_lin'. OR simpler: recompute u_lin_spun for slave dofs via T @ ... no — the spun state is not in the image of T (rigid spin of a constrained structure with supports isn't reducible