 = sum w Log(Q R_i) ≠ Q theta_lin in general! \n\nHmm. So the attachment point x_b is NOT exactly equivariant with the new map either?? Wait — the review's forward-map obligation: \"translation correction is (R_mean-I)*r0 - skew(theta_lin)*r0, not merely (R_mean-I-skew(theta_m))*r0.\" So the review's adopted forward map keeps the -theta_lin × r_0 term. And the contract: \"weighted deformed attachment point and orientation must transform under a common superposed rigid rotation, with the existing linearized weights\". \n\nLet me recheck the review's infinitesimal analysis: \"The current map produces an additive slave-rotation error D*Omega and a slave translation error A*D*Omega relative to a true physical rigid spin.\" So with the old map, translation error = A D Omega where D = sum w J_i^{-1} - J_b^{-1}. With the new map: the mean removes the D error (sum G_i J_i^{-1} = J_m^{-1}). Let me redo the infinitesimal translation for the NEW map:\n\ndu_b under spin Omega: d(sum w u_i) = Omega × sum w x_i (rigid spin of positions: delta x_i = Omega × x_i). d[(R_m - I) r_0] = A(theta_m) dtheta_m = A J_m^{-1} Omega (using dtheta_m = J_m^{-1} Omega — the differential identity!). d[-theta_lin × r_0] = -dtheta_lin × r_0 = -(sum w J_i^{-1} Omega) × r_0.\n\nTrue rigid spin of x_b: Omega × x_b = Omega × (sum w x_i + r_0 + (R_m - I) r_0 ... wait x_b deformed = X_b + u_b; spin: Omega × x_b.\n\ndelta x_b (map) = Omega × sum w x_i + A J_m^{-1} Omega - (sum w J_i^{-1} Omega) × r_0.\n\nHmm wait — I need to be careful about what \"x_i\" is here: deformed master positions. And the term A J_m^{-1} Omega: A = d(R_m r_0)/dtheta_m... A J_m^{-1} Omega = Omega × (R_m r_0) (the review states this: \"This follows from A*J_b^(-1)*Omega = Omega cross (R_b*r0)\"). \n\nTrue: Omega × x_b = Omega × [sum w x_i + R_m r_0] (deformed attachment = weighted master position + rotated offset; since x_b = sum w x_i + (R_m - I) r_0 + ... hmm wait:\n\ndeformed x_b = X_b + u_b = sum w X_i + r_0 + sum w u_i + (R_m - I) r_0 - theta_lin × r_0\n             = sum w x_i + R_m r_0 - theta_lin × r_0.\n\nInteresting — so deformed x_b = sum w (deformed x_i) + R_m r_0 - theta_lin × r_0. The -theta_lin × r_0 term breaks exact equivariance unless theta_lin × r_0 spins equivariantly!\n\nUnder spin: theta_lin → theta_lin + sum w J_i^{-1} Omega. The term -theta_lin × r_0 changes by -(sum w J_i^{-1} Omega) × r_0, which is first order in Omega but NOT equal to -Omega × (theta_lin × r_0)... \n\nHmm wait — but the review's infinitesimal analysis says the current map's translation error is A*D*Omega, where D = sum w J_i^{-1} - J_b^{-1}. Let me recompute for the current (old) map: old x_b = sum w x_i + R(theta_bar) r_0 (since old u_b = sum w u_i + (R(theta_bar)-I) r_0, so deformed x_b = sum w x_i + R_b r_0 — no theta_lin term!). The old map's deformed attachment = sum w x_i + R(theta_bar) r_0. Under spin: delta = Omega × sum w x_i + A[J_bar^{-1} + D] Omega... since dtheta_bar = sum w J_i^{-1} Omega = (J_bar^{-1} + D) Omega. True spin: Omega × x_b = Omega × sum w x_i + Omega × (R_bar r_0) = Omega × sum w x_i + A J_bar^{-1} Omega. Error = A D Omega. ✓ matches review.\n\nSo the OLD map's deformed attachment point is sum w x_i + R(theta_bar) r_0 — the linear theta_lin × r_0 is NOT part of the deformed position (it canceled: X_b = sum w X_i + r_0, and u_b,lin = sum w u_i + theta_lin × r_0 gives deformed = sum w x_i + r_0 + theta_lin × r_0 — the LINEAR deformed attachment; the old nonlinear map replaces it with sum w x_i + R_bar r_0).\n\nNow the NEW map per the review: u_b = sum w u_i + (R_m - I) r_0 - theta_lin × r_0 → deformed x_b = sum w x_i + R_m r_0 - theta_lin × r_0. Hmm — that's NOT sum w x_i + R_m r_0! Why does the review subtract the linear lever?\n\nOH WAIT. I misread the review. Let me re-read: \"Forward map: starting from the old linear expansion, translation correction is (R_mean-I)*r0 - skew(theta_lin)*r0, not merely (R_mean-I-skew(theta_m))*r0.\"\n\n\"Starting from the old linear expansion\" — the correction is applied TO the linear MPC state u_lin (whose slave_u entry already contains sum w u_i + theta_lin × r_0). So physical u_b = u_lin[slave_u] + correction = sum w u_i + theta_lin × r_0 + (R_m - I) r_0 - theta_lin × r_0 = sum w u_i + (R_m - I) r_0. \n\nThe deformed attachment = sum w x_i + R_m r_0. ✓ Equivariant! The \"- skew(theta_lin) r_0\" in the correction removes the linear lever already present in T_linear. My implementation does exactly this: d_u = _nmlr(theta_m) @ r_0 + cross(d_theta, r_0) where _nmlr(theta_m) = R_m - I - skew(theta_m) and cross(d_theta, r_0) = skew(theta_m - theta_lin) r_0. Total correction = (R_m - I) r_0 - skew(theta_m) r_0 + skew(theta_m) r_0 - skew(theta_lin) r_0 = (R_m - I) r_0 - skew(theta_lin) r_0. ✓ \n\nSo in my covariance test, the LINEAR state's slave entry contains the linear lever (from T or set explicitly), and apply adds the correction. Deformed x_b = X_b + u_b = sum w X_i + r_0 + sum w u_i + (R_m - I) r_0 = sum w x_i + R_m r_0. ✓ equivariant given R_m' = Q R_m and sum w x_i' = Q sum w x_i.\n\nSo in the test: x_b = X_slave + u_nl[slave_u]; x_b_spun = X_slave + u_nl_spun[slave_u]; assert x_b_spun == Q @ x_b. ✓ (X_slave unspun reference). And R_b' = Q R_b. ✓\n\nAnd the slave linear entries in u_lin_spun must be the linear MPC values of spun masters (including the linear lever) — as I wrote. ✓\n\nAlso — the review says the map must satisfy \"translation partition of unity\" — sum w u_i part. ✓ by construction.\n\nNow the wrench/moment discriminator test:\n\n```python\ndef test_transfer_preserves_physical_spatial_wrench_interp() -> None:\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\"interpolated\", eccentricity=(0.02, 0.03, -0.06))\n    ... build T, map ...\n    u_lin with distinct master rotations (as above)\n    u_nl = apply(u_lin)\n    imbalance = random full vector with nonzero slave f_b, m_b\n    transferred = map.transfer_slave_imbalance_to_masters(u_nl, imbalance)\n    per entry:\n        f_b, m_b from