   np.testing.assert_allclose(g, J.T @ f, atol=1e-9)\n    # geometric tangent FD: K = d(J^T f - T^T f)/dq\n    K = map.geometric_tangent(u_nl, f)\n    base = g - T.T @ f\n    for k in range(n_red):\n        gp = reduce_force(apply(T@qp+u0), f) - T.T@f\n        gm = ...\n        fd = (gp - gm)/(2h)\n        np.testing.assert_allclose(K.toarray()[:, k], fd, atol=2e-5?)\n```\n\nHmm — FD tolerance: geometric tangent FD with h=1e-7: noise from mean iteration tolerance 1e-14/h=1e-7... The mean converges to ||f||<1e-14 — theta_m error ~1e-14, covector error ~1e-14·|f|, FD derivative error ~1e-14/2e-7 = 5e-8·|f|. With |f| ~ O(1) (random), fine with atol 1e-5. But wait — the mean function's convergence check `<= 1e-14` on ||f||: f is the sum of logs — machine-precision level. Quadratic convergence: reaches ~1e-16 typically. OK.\n\nBut careful — the FD of apply_kinematics wrt q: apply includes the mean; same noise ~1e-14/h = 1e-7. atol 1e-6 fine.\n\nn_red for the fixture: nx=2,ny=1 → shell 3×2=6 nodes... dofs 36 + beam 3 nodes×6=18 → 54 total; constraints: 3 MPC entries × 6 dofs = 18 slave dofs eliminated + supports 2 nodes×6=12 → n_red = 54-18-12=24. FD loop 24 columns × 2 evals × (apply + reduce) — fast.\n\nAlso the existing test at 381 (reduced coupled tangent FD) — parametrized route; runs a solve? Let me check briefly what it does — it FDs the reduced tangent via solves of the model? If it uses _assemble_nonlinear_system with tangent=True and reduce_tangent, it exercises the new geometric tangent. It'll run as part of the suite.\n\nNow — updating the finite-rotation solve test (line 480+). The kinematic relation section and wrench identity section. Let me do a careful edit:\n\nReplace:\n```python\n    # Verify exact nonlinear rotating-arm kinematic relation at all coupled nodes\n    for coupling in meta[\"couplings\"]:\n        slave_dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(coupling[\"slave\"])\n        u_s_bar = np.zeros(3, dtype=float)\n        theta_s_bar = np.zero